# Build context hygiene for docker/Dockerfile (context = repository root).
# Keeps the image build fast and, more importantly, keeps secrets and local
# state out of the layers.

# ---- dependencies & build output (rebuilt inside the image) ----
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- local runtime state: the embedded dev database, uploads, logs ----
**/.runtime
**/.data
**/.tmp
**/storage/local
**/*.log
**/logs

# ---- secrets: never copy a real env file into an image layer ----
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/secrets

# ---- tests, coverage, tooling caches ----
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/.cache
**/.turbo
**/.vite
**/.eslintcache

# ---- VCS / editor / OS ----
.git
.gitignore
.github
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- docs & repo metadata (not needed at runtime) ----
README.md
LICENSE

# NOTE: docker/ is deliberately *not* ignored — BuildKit reads the Dockerfile
# from the build context, so excluding it would break the build.
